On Mar 2, 6:59 am, archmage84 <archmag...@live.com> wrote:
> So let me get this straight: Expert for normal melee weapons
> is stupid unless using #twoweapon (to minimise the penalty),
> Expert for daggers is a very good thing, Expert spellcasting
> schools are excellent too (with exceptions as noted by the
> Wizard page on Wikihack), and #twoweapon is generally awesome?

It's far more complicated than that, but...

 -- If you can get to expert in a ranged weapon with multi-throw
    possibilities, that should always be a priority.

 -- If you can get to skilled in spells where that makes a
    difference, do so.

 -- If you can #twoweapon, it's worth advancing that to skilled,
    along with the slot of your primary weapon.

 -- Beyond that, the difference between skilled and expert isn't
    enormous, but if you have nothing else to do with the slots,
    why not?

At least, that's the way I play it, and it seems to work pretty
well.

